{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"10b29e13-622e-4876-8db0-ff9d6df00e4a","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The generator has been fixed, and details of the changes and colleague note analysis have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-bQYOuD/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Fixed Target Key in [gen.py](file:///tmp/h-bQYOuD/gen.py#L10-L14)**:\n   - Changed `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}` to `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}` in `hr_target()`.\n   - **Why**: Intervals.icu interprets `{value, end}` as a Lap-HR / zone-mapped target, which causes Garmin watches to clamp the corridor to local zone boundaries. Using `{start, end}` designates an Instant-HR corridor, directing Intervals.icu to export the exact calculated bpm target corridor to FIT without watch-side zone clamping.\n\n2. **Documented Analysis in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-bQYOuD/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - **Applied from Colleague's Note**: The `{start, end}` key naming fix for Instant-HR corridors and keeping `units: \"%lthr\"`.\n   - **Ignored from Colleague's Note**: Text grammar formatting rules for the `description` field (since `gen.py` produces the structured JSON `workout_doc` directly) and the live external API/Garmin Connect reproduction instructions.\n","duration_seconds":33.386707,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":111607,"output_tokens":1422,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":4864,"total_tokens":113029}}}
